{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna","id":1530074,"title":"(V5) The Gehenna","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-05T20:47:03-08:00","id":1530074,"title":"(V5) The Gehenna","content":"You see, Vampire - The Masquerade seems like it's really the TTRPG made for me. This underlying idea that there are things out there in which commonners don't fully comprehend - nor should they - just constantly scratches THAT itch for me. Together with that comes that massive dark cloud in the distance, slowly creeping towards the watcher, as the wind blows stronger and the air gets colder. For the common men and women of the world, that could very well be vampires, werewolves and - God forbid - the Wraiths. Now, for the vampires, that's certainly Gehenna.<br /> <br /> You see, something about this paranoid fever of impending doom that the concept of Gehenna brings just scratches THAT itch for me, but unfortunately, I really don't like the way White Wolf handled it in their past materials - from what I know, of course. You see, I don't like the idea that Tzimisce is basically New York's sewers and Ennoia literally becoming one with planet Earth, but I really love this idea that there is a &quot;World of Darkness&quot; and a &quot;World of Darker Darkness&quot;, and that there are things even the Garou should dread to face. With that in mind, the main plot behind my campaign is the lurking paranoia that the signs of Gehenna may cause in the World of Darkness. Lovecraftian much!<br /> <br /> Gladly, I know just how to build that (I'd say it's my specialty making mindfucks out of ideas) and how to engage the players on discovering more and more about this broader scope of things, involving Garous and Wraiths (which have an immense interconnected importance to my story). My problem is in handling Gehenna itself, if it ever comes to happen. One of my favorite things in Vampire - The Masquerade (and even more so in Requiem) is the low-fantasy aspect of all of it, how it's supernatural and mysterious, but still grounded on a palpable reality. I like to think that the fantasy one come to expect from things like D&amp;D, for example, is the wonders and subsequent terror of looking up in the night sky and seeing the infinitude of the vast space; VtM is the wonders and subsequent terror of looking down the abyss and find something slowly creeping back to you from it.<br /> <br /> Without rambling on even more about my lovecraftian ideas, I'd really like Gehenna to happen in my campaign, without actually blowing up the Earth, but giving her a taste of what an actual World War III could cause the planet. How could I &quot;stare down the abyss&quot; but keep it in the low, palpable, fantasy that I've described?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28353-nicknickeo","name":"NickNickeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28353_4.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T20:56:25-08:00","id":1530075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickNickeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna#post1530074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see, Vampire - The Masquerade seems like it's really the TTRPG made for me. This underlying idea that there are things out there in which commonners don't fully comprehend - nor should they - just constantly scratches THAT itch for me. Together with that comes that massive dark cloud in the distance, slowly creeping towards the watcher, as the wind blows stronger and the air gets colder. For the common men and women of the world, that could very well be vampires, werewolves and - God forbid - the Wraiths. Now, for the vampires, that's certainly Gehenna.<br /> <br /> You see, something about this paranoid fever of impending doom that the concept of Gehenna brings just scratches THAT itch for me, but unfortunately, I really don't like the way White Wolf handled it in their past materials - from what I know, of course. You see, I don't like the idea that Tzimisce is basically New York's sewers and Ennoia literally becoming one with planet Earth, but I really love this idea that there is a &quot;World of Darkness&quot; and a &quot;World of Darker Darkness&quot;, and that there are things even the Garou should dread to face. With that in mind, the main plot behind my campaign is the lurking paranoia that the signs of Gehenna may cause in the World of Darkness. Lovecraftian much!<br /> <br /> Gladly, I know just how to build that (I'd say it's my specialty making mindfucks out of ideas) and how to engage the players on discovering more and more about this broader scope of things, involving Garous and Wraiths (which have an immense interconnected importance to my story). My problem is in handling Gehenna itself, if it ever comes to happen. One of my favorite things in Vampire - The Masquerade (and even more so in Requiem) is the low-fantasy aspect of all of it, how it's supernatural and mysterious, but still grounded on a palpable reality. I like to think that the fantasy one come to expect from things like D&amp;D, for example, is the wonders and subsequent terror of looking up in the night sky and seeing the infinitude of the vast space; VtM is the wonders and subsequent terror of looking down the abyss and find something slowly creeping back to you from it.<br /> <br /> Without rambling on even more about my lovecraftian ideas, I'd really like Gehenna to happen in my campaign, without actually blowing up the Earth, but giving her a taste of what an actual World War III could cause the planet. How could I &quot;stare down the abyss&quot; but keep it in the low, palpable, fantasy that I've described?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beckoning is Gehenna in my games.<br /> <br /> The Antediluvians don't want to eat all vampires. Just the tasty old ones that don't meet their standards.<br /> <br /> So the Elders satisfy them until the next cycle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T21:58:12-08:00","id":1530078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickNickeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna#post1530074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without rambling on even more about my lovecraftian ideas, I'd really like Gehenna to happen in my campaign, without actually blowing up the Earth, but giving her a taste of what an actual World War III could cause the planet. How could I &quot;stare down the abyss&quot; but keep it in the low, palpable, fantasy that I've described?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you may want is some kind of event foretold in vampire &quot;prophecy&quot; that is something that must happen in order for Gehenna to occur. Thus you have the foretelling of prophecy happening, but not needing it to result in the End Times. It's simply a sign that Gehenna will in fact be happening sometime in the future. A necessary stop along the way. Perhaps its something stated in your chronicle's version of the Book of Nod (for ideas you may want to consult the Gehenna cults in the Elysium sourcebook), or in some kind of recognized semi-authority apocrypha like a text addendum to the Book of Nod (which may not be widely accepted by Noddist scholars) or a result of &quot;visionaries&quot; like a Malkavian prophet or other figure.<br /> <br /> I think using some kind of Gehenna cult as an active force in your chronicle might do the trick for you. It allows you to introduce some members of the cult early in your chronicle and be relatively normal, but the cult can later be used to explain strange events to come or recruit the PCs as allies or cat's paws in its intrigues. In terms of the actual event used, that is really up to you. Although I think having some slumbering Methusaleh rise at the end of your chronicle and demonstrating its vast powers before the chronicle ends (possibly, but not necessarily, by the PCs destroying the threat) is one option.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T05:14:23-08:00","id":1530089,"title":"","content":"A low-key Gehenna might just be The Withering, or The Beckoning, or something like that. A creeping dread that things are *wrong* and aren't working as they're supposed to, rather than a big crunch that ends the world.<br /> <br /> You could also go super individual with it, and have Caine visit Kindred one by one to judge them. If they fail, they just disappear. He doesn't do it in any order that makes sense, so it could happen to any vampire at any time.<br /> <br /> If you want to build up to it, have the coterie investigate strange vampiric disappearances around the world. Perhaps each one is connected by a symbol or telltale sign that was left behind.<br /> <br /> Only once the characters start to realise that they might be next do you reveal that it's Caine -- and then the panic sets in!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T12:13:53-08:00","id":1530105,"title":"","content":"My fellow Kindred, your help was a blessing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530089#post1530089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A creeping dread that things are *wrong* and aren't working as they're supposed to, rather than a big crunch that ends the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This is what my campaign is all about. Wraiths are being brought back into the body of living things, during 2020s COVID pandemic; a stange cult of Werewolf-worshipping mortals organize themselves in holy rituals in a failing attempt to call the Garou back; and traces of the mysterious and long-gone Salubri are all around the place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530075#post1530075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beckoning is Gehenna in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530089#post1530089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A low-key Gehenna might just be The Withering, or The Beckoning, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. It never crossed my mind that the Beckoning could be Gehenna. It has the mystery, dread and inevitability that I'm looking for. However, I can't seem to grasp how I'd make it a &quot;World of Darkness&quot; problem, and not the impending doom of growing older. Could it be that by consuming the Elders, the Antediluvians grow stronger and THEN they become a worldwide problem? Or do you have something else in mind?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530089#post1530089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could also go super individual with it, and have Caine visit Kindred one by one to judge them. If they fail, they just disappear. He doesn't do it in any order that makes sense, so it could happen to any vampire at any time.<br /> <br /> If you want to build up to it, have the coterie investigate strange vampiric disappearances around the world. Perhaps each one is connected by a symbol or telltale sign that was left behind.<br /> <br /> Only once the characters start to realise that they might be next do you reveal that it's Caine -- and then the panic sets in!</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit that would be metal as Hell, but unfortunately I can't help but think this would be the ultimate Game Over to my campaign. And I don't want it... not yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Re-reading your comment made me realize that the &quot;any vampire, at any time&quot; could be a Hell of a plot. Even though I might not hluse The Father himself, I'm definitely using this with something as scary as the concept of Caine. Thanks a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530078#post1530078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you may want is some kind of event foretold in vampire &quot;prophecy&quot; that is something that must happen in order for Gehenna to occur. Thus you have the foretelling of prophecy happening, but not needing it to result in the End Times. It's simply a sign that Gehenna will in fact be happening sometime in the future. A necessary stop along the way. Perhaps its something stated in your chronicle's version of the Book of Nod (for ideas you may want to consult the Gehenna cults in the Elysium sourcebook), or in some kind of recognized semi-authority apocrypha like a text addendum to the Book of Nod (which may not be widely accepted by Noddist scholars) or a result of &quot;visionaries&quot; like a Malkavian prophet or other figure.<br /> <br /> I think using some kind of Gehenna cult as an active force in your chronicle might do the trick for you. It allows you to introduce some members of the cult early in your chronicle and be relatively normal, but the cult can later be used to explain strange events to come or recruit the PCs as allies or cat's paws in its intrigues. In terms of the actual event used, that is really up to you. Although I think having some slumbering Methusaleh rise at the end of your chronicle and demonstrating its vast powers before the chronicle ends (possibly, but not necessarily, by the PCs destroying the threat) is one option.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now this... this is almost like you're in my campaign yourself. I've got basically everything you've mentioned covered there. The cult, the prophecies and, of course, the prophets. I'm happy that this is something that works from another perspective other than mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28353-nicknickeo","user":"NickNickeo","date":". 02-06-2024, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28353-nicknickeo","name":"NickNickeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28353_4.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T12:49:03-08:00","id":1530106,"title":"","content":"Omens like flocks of bloodless dead animals; Marine animals such as sharks and whales torn to pieces; strange creatures spotted in the sewers; unconfirmed sightings of strange creatures or moving shadows in hapless neighborhoods and on subways. Does this act as signs that something bad is going to happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T16:09:01-08:00","id":1530118,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that the Beckoning is a subtle culling of the clans by the antidulvians who are not impressed with the sort of &quot;people&quot; who got embraced into the family or they made a mockery of whatever they still believe in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:13:35-08:00","id":1530170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickNickeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530105#post1530105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. This is what my campaign is all about. Wraiths are being brought back into the body of living things, during 2020s COVID pandemic; a stange cult of Werewolf-worshipping mortals organize themselves in holy rituals in a failing attempt to call the Garou back; and traces of the mysterious and long-gone Salubri are all around the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is similar to Vampire's Revised Era, really. Especially the later books. Pick up Time of Thin Blood and Nights of Prophecy, if you don't have them. Anything can be a sign of Gehenna if you're paranoid enough.<br /> <br /> You can also go the Blade route, and just have someone attempt a ritual to summon Caine/Lilith/Tzimisce/whatever, and your PCs have to stop them. It might not even be the right being that comes through -- it could be some gibbering thing of mouths and tongues, that upends their whole view of the (Cainite) world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interesting. It never crossed my mind that the Beckoning could be Gehenna. It has the mystery, dread and inevitability that I'm looking for. However, I can't seem to grasp how I'd make it a &quot;World of Darkness&quot; problem, and not the impending doom of growing older. Could it be that by consuming the Elders, the Antediluvians grow stronger and THEN they become a worldwide problem? Or do you have something else in mind? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I would have it ramping up to something. The Withering could be God's judgment; the Beckoning could be the Antediluvians building their strength for a final blow. Or Caine. Or Lilith. Or both of them.<br /> <br /> Maybe Caine and Lilith are each drawing elders to them like some kind of epic game of Pok\u00e9mon! Then, when their armies are assembled, they can duke it out.<br /> <br /> The early 2000s Night Watch film (Russian supernaturals fighting for the chosen one who'll tip the balance in favour of either light or dark) could be a good source of inspiration for that last idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to admit that would be metal as Hell, but unfortunately I can't help but think this would be the ultimate Game Over to my campaign. And I don't want it... not yet. </div> </div> </div>Can Caine be reasoned with? Maybe you can delay him. Maybe he's judging everyone because he's still torn up about Zillah. If you can bring Zillah back, he'll go off into the sunset with her.<br /> <br /> Which means trying to find the Lost Tribe, at the very least...<br /> <br /> Or maybe you can set something equally awful against him.<br /> <br /> But I like the idea of Caine just doing his thing and nobody being able to stop him. It doesn't mean he has to have a deadline -- he could be happy doing this for the next 10,000 years, for all we know.<br /> <br /> All of sudden, every clan has its own version of the Nictuku to worry about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Re-reading your comment made me realize that the &quot;any vampire, at any time&quot; could be a Hell of a plot. Even though I might not hluse The Father himself, I'm definitely using this with something as scary as the concept of Caine. Thanks a lot. </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. Let me know how it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:31:52-08:00","id":1530176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530106#post1530106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Omens like flocks of bloodless dead animals; Marine animals such as sharks and whales torn to pieces; strange creatures spotted in the sewers; unconfirmed sightings of strange creatures or moving shadows in hapless neighborhoods and on subways. Does this act as signs that something bad is going to happen?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure it damn well does. LOL<br /> As a matter of fact, to a lesser extent, this has already happened. Like I said, building up to it is quite easy for me, as I love to play with the mind of players. My problem with Gehenna was The Happening itself, how this supposed war would actually play out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530170#post1530170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> This is similar to Vampire's Revised Era, really. Especially the later books. Pick up Time of Thin Blood and Nights of Prophecy, if you don't have them. Anything can be a sign of Gehenna if you're paranoid enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notes taken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530170#post1530170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Yeah, I would have it ramping up to something. The Withering could be God's judgment; the Beckoning could be the Antediluvians building their strength for a final blow. Or Caine. Or Lilith. Or both of them.<br /> <br /> Maybe Caine and Lilith are each drawing elders to them like some kind of epic game of Pok\u00e9mon! Then, when their armies are assembled, they can duke it out.<br /> <br /> The early 2000s Night Watch film (Russian supernaturals fighting for the chosen one who'll tip the balance in favour of either light or dark) could be a good source of inspiration for that last idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can Caine be reasoned with? Maybe you can delay him. Maybe he's judging everyone because he's still torn up about Zillah. If you can bring Zillah back, he'll go off into the sunset with her.<br /> <br /> Which means trying to find the Lost Tribe, at the very least...<br /> <br /> Or maybe you can set something equally awful against him.<br /> <br /> But I like the idea of Caine just doing his thing and nobody being able to stop him. It doesn't mean he has to have a deadline -- he could be happy doing this for the next 10,000 years, for all we know.<br /> <br /> All of sudden, every clan has its own version of the Nictuku to worry about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're welcome. Let me know how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> Now that you talked about it, I've really liked the idea of The Withering being the seeds of The Beckoning, specially since the only known &quot;panacea&quot; to The Withering is diablerie. And if we want to go really hard into the &quot;doomed&quot; timeline, The Withering could very well be the announcement of Caine's return. Something on the curse of the blood seems to fade away when The Father returns. <br /> <br /> But yeah, as practically everyone who contributed to this post pointed out, The Beckoning is definitely a piece of plot that would work very well with what I'm planning.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28353-nicknickeo","name":"NickNickeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28353_4.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T14:12:09-08:00","id":1530313,"title":"","content":"The Beckoning is a useful plot device to exclude or include potent elders in your game and I can live with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T10:02:58-07:00","id":1536437,"title":"","content":"I think what you need to implement your Gehenna, here, is to answer a simpler question: what you want to change in the setting for the rest of your game?<br /> <br /> Making the Gehenna happen without ending the overall street level tone isn't as hard as it seems. You just have to define what scar it will leave in the world as the Kindred now it.<br /> <br /> You can draw elements from Requiem, for example. It may be VII, a murderous group killing Kindred without rime or reason, but absolutely unstoppable. It may be the actual Disciplines changing, everyone noticing but completely clueless about how or why.<br /> <br /> One book I really recommend for you isn't even WoD, but D&amp;D 3.5: <b><i>Elder Evils</i></b>. This is one of the best books I've ever read about making apocalyptic plots, and the main ideas and mechanics are easy to translate to any system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T12:10:33-07:00","id":1536450,"title":"","content":"Our game we have Elders that have been Beckoned and either they come back much stronger or shockingly much weaker if they return at all and it upsets the status quo of our city as many of the anciellae and older neonates have taken advantage of there absence and staked there claim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T21:11:01-07:00","id":1536918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530074-v5-the-gehenna?p=1530118#post1530118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that the Beckoning is a subtle culling of the clans by the antidulvians who are not impressed with the sort of &quot;people&quot; who got embraced into the family or they made a mockery of whatever they still believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always seen it as what's always been blatantly stated in the metafiction: the Antediluvians main reason for creating their &quot;Clans&quot; is as a source of food when they awaken from torpor. There are no witnesses left, because they can all drain their progeny remotely. Then they make new 4th gens, take a 2,000 year old nap, then it starts again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:09:36-07:00","id":1537013,"title":"","content":"To me metaplots are just suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}